sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, rule 5 (merge into node.role_converge: a version pin is a role setting), DECISIONS R1-R4. docs/reference/analytics.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: analytics:update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 21<br/>analytics role
  CLI->>GW: analytics:update 3.2.1<br/>Plausible version
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit analytics:update 3.2.1`
  %%> - syntax: `[version] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Plausible Community Edition version as three numbers; the image tag is `v` plus the version
  %%> - in a terminal the CLI asks for a missing version; with `--json` it refuses (`analytics.version_invalid`)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - changes the `analytics` role's version setting and converges the role
  Note over GW: Validate the version<br/>role setting · role lock
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway Node
  %%> - a Node has the active `analytics` role (`analytics.role_missing`)
  %%> - no other change runs for that role; the Gateway holds one lock
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether the version differs from the one that runs
  alt same version
    Note over GW: Nothing to change<br/>R1: no run
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing changes; no Swamp run starts (R1)
    GW-->>CLI: Version unchanged<br/>3.2.1 on Node 21
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once
  else another version
    GW->>SW: Start role converge<br/>operation-node-role · analytics
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - records task #5128 as `node.role_converge` for Node 21's `analytics` role, with the new version as its setting
    %%> - pushes the Plausible environment to the Swamp vault after commit (R3) and starts one run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the new and the current `plausible` Process definitions, and the vault key name of the environment
    %%> - Node 21's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    %%> Why no own kind:
    %%> - a version pin is a role setting; the role converge already replaces the Process (rule 5)
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5128
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Prepare the database<br/>createdb · migrate (new image)
    %%> How:
    %%> - over SSH from 209 with `@swamp/ssh`, reading the environment with `vault.get`
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs the new image's `createdb` and `migrate` as one-off containers; the running Process keeps serving
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the old container keeps running unchanged
    SW->>N: Replace the Process<br/>same shape as process.update
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the old `plausible` container and creates it from the new image, with the same environment and mounts
    %%> Why it is safe:
    %%> - Plausible keeps no data in its container
    SW->>N: Check Plausible is healthy<br/>owned spec · HTTP answers
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks the container runs the new image and Plausible answers over HTTP
    alt the check passes
      N-->>SW: Plausible ready
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - Plausible runs the new version
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Record the version<br/>3.2.1 · task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the role's version becomes 3.2.1 and the Process definition is updated
      %%> - task #5128 succeeds
    else replacing or the check fails
      N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no answer
      %%> When:
      %%> - the new container does not start or Plausible does not answer
      SW->>N: Restore the old Process<br/>previous image and spec
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - removes the failed container and creates it again from the captured previous definition, then checks it answers
      %%> Not reversed:
      %%> - the database migrations
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed, its error code, and whether the restore passed
      Note over GW: Keep the old version<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the role keeps its previous version; task #5128 fails
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5128
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
